.git
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
dist/
*.egg-info/
data/
.env
# `.env` above is anchored at the context root. An env file anywhere else (Vite reads
# `webui/.env*`) must not reach an image layer either; the committed templates may.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.db

# Not code, and some of it is local/personal: keep it out of the published image.
webui/node_modules/
# The image builds the console itself (Dockerfile, `webui` stage). The `dist/` entry
# above is anchored at the context root and does not match this directory, so without
# this line `COPY . .` would carry a stale local build into the image.
webui/dist/
# The wheel's packaged copy of the build (scripts/bundle_webui.py), for the same reason.
src/iris_harness/server/iris_api/webui_dist/
htmlcov/
graphify-out/
~/
.phase2-baselines/
.benchmarks/
scenarios/results/
docs/testing-program/results/

# build_image.sh builds from the Mac checkout, which also holds Claude Code's agent
# worktrees (.claude/worktrees/*: full repo copies, each with its own data/ and .venv,
# which the root-anchored `data/`, `.venv` and `*.db` lines above do not match) and
# local editor/tool state. None of it belongs in an image.
.claude/
.vscode/
.coverage
.import_linter_cache/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
